<section id="data-view" class="view" hidden>
  <header class="page-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">05 / SOURCES & ASSUMPTIONS</p><h1>Behind the ledger.</h1><p class="subtitle">A database of transactions and metadata, with a record of where each import came from.</p></div></header>
  <div class="detail-grid"><article class="card"><h2>Your ledger database</h2><div id="data-details"></div><button id="reload-button" class="outline-button">↺ Refresh ledger</button></article><article class="card"><h2>Import data</h2><p class="input-note">Bank CSV imports add transactions, account names, categories and sender/receiver metadata. Canonical JSON imports can add or update these independently. Reimporting the same source keeps existing transactions and corrections.</p><label>Import format<select id="ingest-adapter"><option value="auto">Detect from file extension</option><option value="norwegian-bank-csv">Norwegian bank CSV</option><option value="canonical-v1">Canonical JSON (transactions + metadata)</option></select></label><button id="data-import-button" class="outline-button">↑ Select import file</button><p id="ingest-status" class="input-note" aria-live="polite"></p><div id="ingest-history"></div></article></div>
  <article class="card"><div class="card-heading"><h2>Export your complete ledger</h2><span class="badge">All saved data</span></div><p>Transactions, accounts, every dated balance, categories, counterparties, corrections, forecast settings and import history.</p><div class="export-actions"><button id="export-ledger-json" class="outline-button">↓ JSON archive</button><button id="export-ledger-sqlite" class="outline-button">↓ SQLite backup</button></div><p class="input-note">Choose JSON for a readable archive or your own tools. Choose SQLite for a complete database restore. Pending saves finish before the download starts.</p><p class="input-note">These private files include account identifiers and original import rows. Sign-in credentials and this browser’s appearance preferences are excluded.</p><p id="ledger-export-status" class="input-note" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></article>
  <article class="card"><div class="card-heading"><h2>Accounts in this ledger</h2><button class="text-button" data-view="accounts">Manage balances →</button></div><div id="account-details"></div><p class="input-note">Account identifiers are matched inside the private database. Payment descriptions remain as supplied by the source.</p></article>
  <article class="card method-card"><h2>What the numbers mean</h2><dl><dt>Money in</dt><dd>All positive amounts except transfers between named accounts. It can include salary, refunds, loan proceeds, and incoming transfers. Forecast regular income uses salary rows only.</dd><dt>Spending</dt><dd>Negative amounts except internal transfers and rows classified as external savings. Loan repayments remain cash outflows; this view does not separate principal from interest or calculate net worth.</dd><dt>External savings</dt><dd>Rows tagged “Sparing” and “Mikrospar til …” are shown separately. They reduce available cash, but may still be your money in an account outside this export. Balances in those accounts are unknown.</dd><dt>Internal transfers</dt><dd>Both source and destination account numbers match a named account in the export. These do not count as income or spending, including transfers into a savings account inside the export.</dd><dt>Repeated rows</dt><dd>Identical rows are kept. Multiple identical purchases and micro-saving payments can be real. The export provides no unique bank transaction ID, so duplicates cannot be removed reliably.</dd><dt>Currency</dt><dd>All charts use “Beløp”, the bank's booked NOK amount. Original foreign-currency amounts are not added together.</dd><dt>Private storage</dt><dd>Transactions, dated account balances, imports, forecast settings and edits are stored in the private database. Theme preferences stay in this browser. The source repository and container images contain no financial data. No external fonts, analytics, or AI calls are used.</dd></dl><button id="clear-saved" class="outline-button danger">Reset forecast settings & transaction edits</button></article>
</section>
